   "ruling": "Ruling: scope; project retained. Schedule 1-A line 36b: \"If you are married filing jointly, your spouse has a valid social security number (see instructions), and your spouse was born before January 2, 1961, enter the amount from line 35\"; i1040gi p. 110: \"If you are married, you must file a joint return with your spouse to claim this deduction.\" The English gates line 36b on the spouse entry, and a spouse entry exists only on a joint return: household.roster_ok requires one entry for the spouse exactly when filing jointly and any other roster is refused at household.roster_bad (Form 1040 page 1, \"If joint return, spouse’s first name\"; fixtures stage13.refuse.single_with_spouse and stage13.refuse.joint_without_spouse, both refused at household.roster_bad, witnesses in triage/s179.json). A head of household or other non-joint return with a spouse entry is therefore refused, never given line 35; married filing separately is refused for the whole return at s3.mfs. The model read the line 36b English without the roster refusal located elsewhere."
